    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="G. N. Lewis (1916) described a covalent bond as a pair of electrons shared by two atoms, and each atom as seeking an octet of eight valence electrons. Often several octet-satisfying structures can be drawn for one molecule. Formal charge ranks them: split every bonding pair evenly, count the electrons each atom then owns, and compare with the free atom,">

